################ 2. Self-healing: drift is reverted automatically ################
# Someone changes the cluster by hand, bypassing Git:
$ kubectl scale deploy/gitops-demo -n gitops-demo --replicas=5
deployment.apps/gitops-demo scaled
  TIME    REPLICAS   ARGO-CD
  t+2s    5          Synced
  t+4s    2          Synced

$ kubectl get application gitops-demo -n argocd -o jsonpath="{.status.operationState.message}"
  successfully synced (all tasks run)
#   Git says 2 replicas, so the cluster goes back to 2. The manual change is undone.

# The same for a deleted resource:
$ kubectl delete service gitops-demo -n gitops-demo
service "gitops-demo" deleted from gitops-demo namespace
$ kubectl get service gitops-demo -n gitops-demo
  gitops-demo  ClusterIP  10.43.182.224  9898/TCP   <- recreated by Argo CD
